WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:03.613
Unit twenty-one. Password Managers!

2
00:00:04.574 --> 00:00:09.678
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:09.728 --> 00:00:13.704
Hi, Mr. Daniel! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:13.754 --> 00:00:18.081
Today we learn about Password Managers. Let's go!

5
00:00:19.429 --> 00:00:24.029
Password manager. Say it with me. Password manager!

6
00:00:27.577 --> 00:00:32.277
Master password. Say it with me. Master password!

7
00:00:35.733 --> 00:00:39.399
Unique. Say it with me. Unique!

8
00:00:42.895 --> 00:00:46.395
Generate. Say it with me. Generate!

9
00:00:49.979 --> 00:00:53.812
Encrypted. Say it with me. Encrypted!

10
00:00:57.248 --> 00:01:00.614
Vault. Say it with me. Vault!

11
00:01:04.154 --> 00:01:08.147
Autofill. Say it with me. Autofill!

12
00:01:11.641 --> 00:01:15.721
Security. Say it with me. Security!

13
00:01:19.251 --> 00:01:29.513
A password manager stores passwords in an encrypted vault. It can generate a unique password for every site and autofill it. You only remember one strong master password.

14
00:01:29.563 --> 00:01:32.851
Now I understand. Thank you, Mr. Daniel!

15
00:01:34.101 --> 00:01:39.278
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:39.328 --> 00:01:40.478
Unique!

17
00:01:41.528 --> 00:01:46.773
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:46.823 --> 00:01:47.973
Autofill!

19
00:01:49.071 --> 00:01:56.797
Did you know? Using a unique password for every account stops one data leak from affecting all your accounts!

20
00:01:56.847 --> 00:01:59.262
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:08.625
Think and answer. What are the benefits of using a password manager?

22
00:02:08.675 --> 00:02:09.825
Great answer!

23
00:02:10.914 --> 00:02:16.221
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:16.271 --> 00:02:19.448
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

